\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Arrival-time rounding and numerical resolution. (a) Angular change caused by rounding analytical arrivals for an array radius of 0.05 m and a source distance of 1.5 m. Exact spherical arrivals are processed by the same plane-wave direction solver, and the curves exclude waveform noise. (b) Largest angular changes under numerical refinement on the fixed 24-scene subset, using five recordings and 32 frames per scene. The dashed line marks the $0.05^\circ $ numerical target.}}{7}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:numerics}{{2}{7}{Arrival-time rounding and numerical resolution. (a) Angular change caused by rounding analytical arrivals for an array radius of 0.05 m and a source distance of 1.5 m. Exact spherical arrivals are processed by the same plane-wave direction solver, and the curves exclude waveform noise. (b) Largest angular changes under numerical refinement on the fixed 24-scene subset, using five recordings and 32 frames per scene. The dashed line marks the $0.05^\circ $ numerical target}{figure.2}{}}
